// Tibetan (bo) — Standard / Lhasa Tibetan, Tibetan script. One of the DEEPEST orthographies in the world: a
// syllable-stack RULE ENGINE (prefix·superscript·root·subscript·vowel·suffix → tonogenetic tone + onset-cluster
// realization + suffix-driven vowel umlaut/length/nasalization). PRIMARY = hand-curated JIPA "Central Tibetan
// (Lhasa)" illustration (INDEPENDENT, CC-BY, 40 pairs). SECONDARY = kaikki Lhasa (1281) which is MODULE-GENERATED
// (Module:bo-pron) → REFERENCE-PARITY, disclosed. Independent COVERAGE separately validated at 100% of tokens on
// 300k TIBMD@MUC Lhasa syllables (numerals aside). Tone (2-level ˥/˩), length, ties, combining accents are stripped
// by the shared BACKBONE (segmental cf, like hmn/cdo/yue); tone is asserted in test/tibetan.test.ts.
