    "secondaryGap": "The PRIMARY is the small INDEPENDENT JIPA human anchor (40). The large kaikki secondary (1281) is MODULE-GENERATED (Module:bo-pron) → reference-parity, NOT independent, so it is reported not floored. It is further DEFLATED (~raw 22%) by principled divergence we do NOT chase: (a) the -d/-g/-s CHECKED coda — we emit ʔ (the JIPA careful register) vs the module's colloquial vowel-LENGTH; (b) per-syllable contour-tone notation. Independent breadth instead comes from TIBMD@MUC (OpenSLR 124, Minzu Univ., non-Wiktionary): 100% of 299,733 Lhasa syllable tokens phonemize cleanly (coverage, not IPA-accuracy — TIBMD ships transcripts, no pron-dict).",
